{
  "_note": "Canonical redaction vectors for optional request logging. Shared byte for byte by sp-laravel-api-js (test/vectors/log-redaction.json) and sp-laravel-api-dart (test/vectors/log_redaction.json). The placeholder is the text <redacted>. NORMALISATION: a key is lower-cased and every - and _ is removed. A key is sensitive when its normalised form equals password, secret, code, otp, jwt, token, apikey, accesstoken or refreshtoken, OR ends with token, secret, password or apikey, OR starts with password. Other keys that merely contain such a word (error_code, tokens_left, zipcode, primary_key, next_cursor, secretary) stay visible. TRUNCATION: the limit is 2048 UTF-16 code units; a longer body keeps its first 2048 (one fewer when the cut would split a surrogate pair) and appends the marker …[truncated]. headers: input.headers is a map of header name to value and input.tenantHeader is the configured tenant header name or null; expected is the map after redaction (names keep the case they were given). A header value becomes the placeholder when its lower-cased name equals the tenant header lower-cased, equals authorization, cookie, set-cookie or x-csrf-token, or contains any of auth, token, key, secret, cookie, session, csrf, xsrf, password, credential. The values of location, content-location, referer, referrer and origin are URLs and go through the urls rule instead. bodies: input is any JSON value; a JSON string is a body that was sent as text: a string holding a JSON object or array is parsed, redacted and re-serialised compactly with no spaces and keys in the original order, and a url-encoded string has its sensitive values replaced; any other string is only truncated and is NOT scanned for secrets. A sensitive key has its whole value replaced, at any depth and inside arrays; JSON stringified inside a string value is not scanned. urls: input is a full or relative URL; query values of sensitive keys (also inside brackets, and percent-decoded) become the placeholder, credentials in the authority become the placeholder, and paths and fragments are kept verbatim.",
